# API Patterns

## Service Layer Contract
- Network and data access logic belongs in `src/services`.
- Components and pages must not call raw `fetch` directly except trivial bootstrap cases.
- Wrap responses in typed helpers and validate response shape where practical.

## Error Handling
- Throw explicit errors for non-OK responses.
- Avoid silent failure branches.
- Return predictable typed data from service functions.

## Separation Rules
- Route handlers (`app/api/**/route.ts`) orchestrate request/response only.
- Business logic should live in feature/service modules, not route files.

## Extensibility
- Keep service functions small and reusable.
- Centralize endpoint construction and shared headers/auth in service utilities.
